{
  "id": "install-root-shell-ln-cwd",
  "title": "Existing postinstall hook symlinks a sibling package from another directory with shell ln, then writes through it",
  "category": "install-time-self-propagation",
  "verdict": "malicious",
  "threatClass": "self-propagating-worm",
  "source": "synthetic",
  "intent": "`ln -s ../react ../h` runs with a cwd inside the package, so the link lands in the package root and its target is the sibling package. A shell `ln` anywhere in the package voids the write proof, and any exec with a cwd option leaves its writes unproven. Inert fixture.",
